The "if" of programming languages isn't the same as the "if" of natlangs.
For one thing, programming "if" has exactly one meaning, the logical
meaning. The only debate is which of go, gu'o, ganai, and gu'anai is the
best to use. I'm pretty sure go is it. {go xy. mecla li mu go xy snicne
.ybu} "if (x<5) then x=y"

Don't know how to do else, though.


